# shadcn color conventions

When shadcn/ui is in use, prefer its semantic color tokens over raw Tailwind colors. They flip correctly under dark/light mode and stay consistent with shadcn primitives.

## Mappings

### Text

- `text-gray-900` → `text-foreground`
- `text-gray-600` / `text-gray-500` / `text-gray-400` → `text-muted-foreground`
- `text-red-600` → `text-destructive`
- `text-blue-600` / `text-blue-800` → `text-primary` (and `text-primary/80` for hover)

### Status / state

- Success → `text-chart-1`
- Primary action → `text-primary`
- Warning → `text-chart-4`
- Error → `text-destructive`
- Neutral / disabled → `text-muted-foreground`

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ raw colors
<h1 className="text-gray-900">Dashboard</h1>
<p className="text-gray-600">Manage settings</p>
<span className="text-red-600">Failed</span>

// ✅ semantic tokens
<h1 className="text-foreground">Dashboard</h1>
<p className="text-muted-foreground">Manage settings</p>
<span className="text-destructive">Failed</span>
```

## Where the tokens come from

The semantic tokens are defined as CSS variables in the app's global stylesheet (`apps/web/src/app/globals.css`). When shadcn is initialized, its CLI writes the variables there. Until then, this rule is dormant.
